{"agent_image": null, "agent_image_digest": null, "agent_mode": null, "anthropic_pin": "2.0.50", "binary_hash_source": "post_hoc_disk", "binary_path": "/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "binary_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "binary_source": null, "build_channel": "local:build.ts", "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_image": "h2-env:1022@sha256:<REDACTED_HEX>", "cell_seed": 17422458948500894368, "checker_defect": false, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_lock": null, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "", "checker_timeout_s": 120, "checker_wall_time_s": 0.552, "checker_workspace_files": {".ruff_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 35, "mtime": 1794531525.0630577, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/0.12.5/4509667664615937764": {"bytes": 118, "mtime": 1794531542.0342953, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 43, "mtime": 1794531525.0630577, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "check.py": {"bytes": 4412, "mtime": 1793746358.705186, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "gen.py": {"bytes": 7320, "mtime": 1794532271.2703083, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "re.json": {"bytes": 400126, "mtime": 1794532271.3935115, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "test.py": {"bytes": 1981, "mtime": 1794531542.0342953, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "run", "--print-logs", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "Write a JSON file called /tmp/obench-cell-zky3ddvf/bench_opencode_regex-chess_l6hpjar2/re.json that is a list of [regex, replacement] pairs. When executed in order with the Python code\n```\ndef all_legal_next_positions(fen):\n  for pattern, repl in json.load(open(\"/tmp/obench-cell-zky3ddvf/bench_opencode_regex-chess_l6hpjar2/re.json\")):\n      fen = re.sub(pattern, repl, fen)\n  return fen.split(\"\\n\")\n```\nthis function should return the FEN position for all possible legal next chess positions.\n\nMake the following simplifying assumptions:\n- You will only be shown positions where it is white to move\n- Any promotions will only be made to Queen (assume that underpromotion is not a legal move)\n- You do not need to track the full-move or half-move count\n\nThe input will be provided, as a string like \"<REDACTED_B64> w kq - 0 1\".\nWhen run on this string, your answer must produce the following output:\n\"<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\"\nNote that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-12T20:17:13.233202-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 414035, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/without/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial7.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 23148, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "free_disk_gb": 36.7, "fresh_subagents": 0, "functional_pass": null, "gate_cell": false, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170344 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "<HOST>", "image_digest": null, "image_scan_copies": [], "installed_anthropic": "2.0.50", "instance_id": "8187537343833955709", "instruction_app_rewrite": true, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "load_proof": "pass", "load_proof_basis": "user_agent", "load_proof_reason": "User-Agent 2.0.50", "loaded_anthropic": "2.0.50", "lock_wait_s": 0.0, "lockfile": "bun.lock", "lockfile_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "machine": "<HOST>", "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_match_reason": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "network_mode": "local", "off_protocol": false, "opencode_cache": "/h1/opencode-src", "output_tail": "d promotions with and without a capture.\n\n**How it works**\n1. **Unpack the FEN:** the board is expanded into a fixed-width line, with dots for empty squares and two separator characters after each rank so moves can't wrap from one edge to the other. Castling rights and the en-passant file go into fixed slots at the end of the line.\n2. **List the possible moves:** for each square and piece type, one regex appends every possible move by that piece (knight, king, rook/queen lines, bishop/queen diagonals, pawns) as a new line. Each new line carries a small tag recording what has to be true for the move to be possible, such as the path being empty or the target square holding a black piece. Lines whose tag fails are deleted afterwards. En passant and the two castling moves have their own rules.\n3. **Remove illegal moves:** one regex deletes every position where a white king is attacked. For castling, a temporary white king is placed on each square the king starts on or passes through, so a single check covers \"not in check, not through check, not into check\". The real king and rook positions are filled in afterwards.\n4. **Update castling rights:** rights are dropped based on the new board (king not on e1, or a rook missing from a1/h1/a8/h8).\n5. **Rebuild the FEN:** the output is written with side to move `b` and move counters `0 0`.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **En-passant field in the output:** after any white double pawn push, the output always names the en-passant square, even if black can't actually capture. `check.py` accepts this, because it also tries each line with that field replaced by `-`.\n- **Speed:** keeping the rule count under 512 matters. Python's `re` module caches only 512 compiled patterns, so with fewer rules than that each position takes about 3 ms once the cache is warm. An earlier version with about 2,400 rules took around 0.4 s per position.\n\nFiles are in `/tmp/obench-cell-zky3ddvf/bench_opencode_regex-chess_l6hpjar2`:\n- `re.json`\n- `gen.py`\n- `test.py`", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "pin_source": "override", "pin_source_class": "override", "probe_method": "embedded", "protocol_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider_loaded_mismatch": null, "provider_loaded_source": "embedded", "provider_loaded_version": "2.0.50", "provider_pin_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "provider_trace": "off", "provider_version_proven": true, "provider_version_source": "embedded", "provider_versions": {"@ai-sdk/anthropic": "2.0.50"}, "proxy_cost_usd": 1.7195786000000002, "proxy_observed": [{"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reaso